WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:02.120
Hey, this is Presh Talwakar.

00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:05.020
Martin is a gardener in Mathland.

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:09.040
There are 100 poisonous flowers
in his garden

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:11.020
that he wants to destroy.

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:12.340
On their own,

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:14.820
the flowers do not change in number.

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:19.060
Martin has a spray to kill
the poisonous flowers,

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:22.440
but the spray works
only in a specific way.

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:27.180
The spray has settings to destroy
exactly 3,

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:31.680
5, 14, or 17 flowers instantly.

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:34.700
The spray only works if

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:37.770
there are at least as many flowers
as the setting.

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:40.960
If there are two flowers, for example,

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:43.280
the setting for 3 does nothing.

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:47.800
Furthermore, if at least
one flower survives

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:49.340
after he sprays them,

00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:51.740
the flowers instantly grow back

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:53.410
based on how many died.

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:57.520
If 3 die, then 12 grow back.

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:00.740
If 5 die, then 17 grow back.

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:04.120
If 14 die, then 8 grow back.

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:07.100
If 17 die, 2 grow back.

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:12.470
If the number of flowers
is ever exactly zero,

00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:15.300
then the flowers never grow back.

00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:18.360
Can Martin ever get rid of the

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:20.760
poisonous flowers in his garden?

00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:24.470
You can assume
he has an unlimited amount of spray.

00:01:25.900 --> 00:01:27.240
Can you figure it out?

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:29.900
Give this problem a try,
and when you're ready,

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:32.380
keep watching the video for the solution.

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:43.420
So, from the initial
100 flowers,

00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:46.880
you can try experimenting
the different combinations

00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:49.000
of the flowers
you can spray,

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:51.360
and keep track of
how many flowers remain.

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:54.120
But no matter how you try,

00:01:54.120 --> 00:01:57.140
you're not gonna be able to 
get rid of all the flowers.

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:00.220
We can understand why

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:02.960
by thinking forward
and reasoning backwards.

00:02:04.580 --> 00:02:06.940
So in order for 
Martin to succeed,

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:12.160
there needs to be
3, 5, 14, or 17 flowers

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:16.160
just before the last time
he sprays the flowers.

00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:20.880
This means 
from the initial 100 flowers,

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:23.840
Martin has to decrease
the number of flowers

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:29.720
by exactly 97, 95, 86,
or 83 flowers.

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:36.180
Let's consider the net change
after each setting of the spray.

00:02:37.060 --> 00:02:39.360
If he uses a setting of 3,

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:43.000
he kills 3,
but 12 grow back,

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:46.480
which leads to plus 9 flowers.

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:49.120
For the setting of 5,

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:52.180
there is a net change
of plus 12 flowers.

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:55.100
For 14 setting,

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:57.300
he decreases the number
of flowers by 6,

00:02:57.580 --> 00:02:59.200
and for the 17 setting,

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:01.780
he decreases the number 
of flowers by 15.

00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:07.560
On each setting of the spray,

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:09.900
Martin can only change the
number of flowers

00:03:10.140 --> 00:03:14.300
by +9, +12, -6, or -15,

00:03:14.680 --> 00:03:16.720
and there's a pattern
to these numbers.

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:20.180
They are all multiples of 3.

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:26.000
Since Martin only changes
the number of flowers

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:27.600
by a multiple of 3,

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:31.380
the number of flowers
has to change by 3x

00:03:31.380 --> 00:03:33.640
for certain integer
values of x.

00:03:36.420 --> 00:03:43.120
Now, since the numbers 97, 95,
86, and 83 are not multiples of 3,

00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:45.360
that means Martin
is not capable

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:47.560
of decreasing the initial number

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:50.080
by exactly any 
of those numbers.

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:53.100
Therefore, we can conclude

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:55.220
Martin can never get rid of

00:03:55.230 --> 00:03:57.710
all of the poisonous flowers.

00:03:58.600 --> 00:04:00.600
Did you figure it out?

